# The generated third-party license document carries each dependency's license
# text exactly as that crate wrote it, and at least one of them uses CRLF. Git
# would otherwise normalize line endings on commit or checkout depending on the
# contributor's `core.autocrlf`, which both rewrites somebody else's license
# text and makes the staleness check in CI fail on a tree nobody changed.
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md -text

# Bundled fonts are binary, and their license texts are shipped exactly as the
# font's author wrote them (some use CRLF), so neither may be re-encoded or
# have line endings rewritten on checkout.
crates/gui/ui/fonts/*.ttf binary
crates/gui/ui/fonts/licenses/* -text
